+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | Draft                |
+
+The tool registry validates model supplied arguments at its execution boundary so tools receive inputs that satisfy their declared JSON Schema.
+
+## Execution contract
+
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` validates input against the registered tool's `inputSchema` before calling the executor; rejected input returns a `ToolResponse` describing the validation failure and does not invoke the executor. ([validated by: rejects input missing a required field before invoking the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L15))
+- Input with a wrong declared type is rejected with a message naming the field and expected type, without exposing the supplied value. ([validated by: rejects a wrong field type without including the supplied value](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L32))
+- Valid input, including unlisted extra properties, reaches the executor unchanged and exactly once. ([validated by: passes valid input and extra properties through unchanged](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L50))
